  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Facts: out, from the phone to ROS",
      "items": [
        "The page sends JSON over its one WebSocket; deliver() hands it on only while that link is the current phone (wsserver.py 196–202).",
        "parse() keeps the known fields of each message type and clamps every number (protocol.py 118–237); anything else is dropped with a warning.",
        "text() publishes standard types where they exist (Imu, Float32, BatteryState) and JSON in a String otherwise; IMU at most 60 Hz, faces 10 Hz, vision MAX_SEE_RATE (bridge_node.py 244–299).",
        "A face's familiar number goes out only while familiar is asked and allowed; otherwise the bridge sets it to null (bridge_node.py 289)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Facts: in, from ROS to the phone",
      "items": [
        "One subscription per in-topic; each goes through out() and a protocol maker that checks and clamps it before it is sent (bridge_node.py 86–99, 120–126).",
        "server.send() gives the phone the message and every mirror a copy (wsserver.py 168–172): diagram 09.",
        "Programs: omi_assist (tiles, the follower, reminders), guardian_node (the Desk Guardian, which also drives the Thymio: cmd_vel out, prox/ground in) and any program; they use only these topics (omi_assist.py 40–48, guardian_node.py 59–73). The setup page's tests publish on the same topics (bridge_node.py 107–111)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Held back from ROS",
      "items": [
        "Pictures: no topic carries a frame. A frame the person shows (Zeigen) goes to the setup page and to loopback mirrors only, and only while showing is allowed (bridge_node.py 335–339).",
        "The screen report goes to the mirrors, not to ROS (bridge_node.py 332–334). The text read aloud stays on the phone: read/result carries counts (contract.py 43).",
        "The location stays on the phone's screen: sensor_report() has no field for it (protocol.py 256–277)."
      ]
    }
  ]
